# schema-install-fallback walks up from its own directory for VERSION, then runs scripts/install.sh into an empty target; install.sh
# copies from core/, patterns/ and templates/ (SCRIPT_DIR/../<tree>), and reads VERSION. The five scripts under test are the ones that
# install lays down at scripts/ai-dlc/, taken from core/scripts/. A fixture's own directory is copied by the runner, never declared.
!scripts/install.sh
# +VERSION: VERSION is a content-key-EXCLUDED top, and run.sh:87 reads it as the walk-up marker, so it is keyed per fixture (I55 arm 3).
+VERSION
# reason: core/ is enumerated -- install.sh (run at run.sh:153) globs core/scripts/*, core/hooks/*.sh, core/schemas/*.json and more, scripts/install.sh:471, :374, :550; run.sh:187 walks the installed scripts.
core/
patterns/
templates/
